L("patterns-in-mathematics","visualising-and-relating-number-sequences","Visualising number sequences and how they relate","Meena arranged dots into squares and triangles on the floor.\n\"The dots show the numbers,\" she said.",
 ["Some sequences can be drawn. Square numbers 1, 4, 9, 16 make square arrangements of dots. Triangular numbers 1, 3, 6, 10 make triangles.","Sequences are related. Adding two neighbouring triangular numbers gives a square number: 3 plus 6 is 9. The sum of the first few odd numbers is a square: 1 plus 3 plus 5 is 9.","Seeing a picture of a pattern helps us explain why it works."],
 ["square number","triangular number","visualise"],("Find the sum of the first 4 odd numbers.",[("The odd numbers are 1, 3, 5, 7.","List."),("1 plus 3 plus 5 plus 7 is 16.","Add."),("16 is the square of 4.","Answer.")]),
 ("1 + 3 + 5 + 7 is 20.",["It equals 16.","The sum of first n odd numbers is n squared."],["Adding wrongly."]),
 ["Pictures show sequences.","Odd numbers add to squares."],
 ["m|Square numbers start 1, 4, 9,|16|12|10|4x4.","t|Triangular numbers are 1, 3, 6, 10.|T|Yes.","m|1 + 3 + 5 =|9|8|10|Square of 3.","t|1 + 3 + 5 + 7 is 20.|F|16.","m|3 + 6 =|9|8|10|Neighbours.","s|Next triangular number after 10? Write only the number.|15|Add 5.","m|Pictures of dots help us|see patterns|forget|sleep|Draw.","t|Odd numbers add up to squares.|T|Yes."])
