 ["A point marks an exact position and has no size. A line segment joins two points and has a fixed length.","A line goes on forever in both directions. A ray starts at one point and goes on forever in one direction, like a torch beam.","Two rays meeting at a common end point form an angle."],
 ["point","line segment","ray"],("How is a ray different from a line segment?",[("A segment has two end points.","Segment."),("A ray has one end point.","Ray."),("A ray goes on forever one way.","Answer.")]),
 ("a line segment goes on forever.",["A line segment has two end points.","A line goes on forever."],["Mixing."]),
 ["Segment has length, line is endless.","Ray has one end point."],
